  {
   "id": "-qfik4cWAwAJ",
   "from": "Vincent van Hees",
   "author": "8d92e34685fbc6bd",
   "date": "2019-11-08T08:37:52Z",
   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] CSV Output - ERROR",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Graydon for reporting back, but I am struggling to follow this because &quot;ndayswindow&quot; is only <a href=\"https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/search?q=ndayswindow&amp;unscoped_q=ndayswindow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wadpac/GGIR/search?q%3Dndayswindow%26unscoped_q%3Dndayswindow&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792491024929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0CsLsH7PGy6JttWk3MovVq\">used</a> when strategy is set to 3. <div>The repetition of data may indicate that the values were imputed because the underlying data was classified as invalid (monitor not worn). What happens if you set do.imp=TRUE, which turns of the imputation?</div><div>Vincent</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, 4 Nov 2019 at 19:03, Graydon Raymer &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gray...@nipissingu.ca</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>I think I found the problem, and the solution. Although I was using “strategy = 1” for Part 2, it looks like the epochvalues2csv is sensitive to what you put as the ndayswindow. If you put a value in dayswindow less than the actual number of days in your data, regardless of the “strategy” the epoch2values setting does not export the epoch values beyond ndayswindow and just repeats the epochs for the last full “ndayswindow” until a time point that would be the end of the data file.<br><div>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br>Graydon Raymer R.Kin, PhD</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Director, School of Physical and Health Education<br>Room 201F, Centre for Physical and Health Education</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Nipissing University<br>100 College Drive, Box 5002<br>North Bay, Ontario P1B 8L7<br>Canada<br>Phone: <a href=\"tel:(705)%20474-3461\" value