normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br>Graydon Raymer R.Kin, PhD</div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Director, School of Physical and Health Education<br>Room 201F, Centre for Physical and Health Education</div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Nipissing University<br>100 College Drive, Box 5002<br>North Bay, Ontario P1B 8L7<br>Canada<br>Phone: <a href=\"tel:(705)%20474-3461\" value=\"+17054743461\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(705) 474-3461 x4449</a></div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Fax: <a href=\"tel:(705)%20495-4573\" value=\"+17054954573\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(705) 495-4573</a><br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Email: gray...@nipissingu.ca</a></div></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Nov 1, 2019, at 3:36 PM, Graydon Raymer &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gray...@nipissingu.ca</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div>Help! — I am using the &quot;epochvalues2csv = TRUE” setting to pull out the individual epoch values (ENMO) for each time point, because I want to calculate ENMO (and other things) for some very specific intervals each day.<div><br></div><div>I’ve noticed a bug in GGIR. The CSV output (found in the output/meta/csv folder) looks correct for the first couple days of my recording. But, after the third day, although the timestamp keeps increasing correctly, the values (both ENMO and anglez) keep repeating over the 24-hour period the same values from day 3.</div><div><br></div><div>See the attached CSV output as an example. Look at June 7, 8, 9, 10 — the output is exactly the same for each of these days!</div><div><br></div><div>Hopefully it’s an easy fix??</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Graydon</div><div><div>\r\n<div style=\"letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br>Graydon Raymer R.Kin, PhD</div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Director, School of Physical and Health Education<br>Room 201F, Centre for Physical and Health Education</div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Nipissing University<br>100 College Drive, Box 5002<br>North Bay, Ontario P1B 8L7<br>Canada<br>Phone: <a href=\"tel:(705)%20474-3461\" value=\"+17054743461\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(705) 47